<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
{# grid rules painted as one anti-aliased fill like this "Microsoft: Print To PDF" original (sars_pdf/rules.py) #}
<meta name="sars-pdf:rules" content="filled-aa">
<title>{{ doc.sections[0].title if doc.sections else 'District performance' }}</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
{#
  Region district performance (LEVEL + FUNCTION name). Region-only, section-centric: one
  per-district division grid per page. Fully self-contained (own template + own style.css,
  inline @font-face, no shared stylesheet). Data-driven and location-agnostic; the
  competency-level background is the ONLY data-driven colour.

  Grid (2 header bands, district rows, TOTAL row):
    S/N | DISTRICT | NUMBER OF SCHOOLS | REGISTERED F M T (only when has_registered)
        | SAT F M T % | I | II | III | IV (F M T) | 0 F M T % | I-III F M T % | I-IV F M T %
        | GPA | COMPETENCY LEVEL | RANK (rotated)

  The original prints every section KIND (overall / government / private / percentage /
  kpi) from its own Excel sheet: its own column widths and its own print scale (fonts,
  row heights, rule weights, title block). Each kind's geometry below is measured from the
  original (rule centres, baselines above the rule centre below, font sizes) and lives
  HERE, in one place. A kind without its own entry falls back to the geometry of the same
  shape (with / without REGISTERED).
#}
